WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:01.401 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It does seem as though
one of the things

00:00:01.401 --> 00:00:03.103
when you talk about how the rich
are being taken care of,

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.405
money is obviously playing
a huge role in politics,

00:00:05.405 --> 00:00:07.040 size:75% position:38%
and I feel as though
the Democratic Party

00:00:07.040 --> 00:00:10.043
also has to answer for the large
amounts of corporate money

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.077 line:92%
they've taken over the years.

00:00:11.077 --> 00:00:12.712 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don't take
corporate PAC money.

00:00:12.712 --> 00:00:14.047 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No.
-But do you think that

00:00:14.047 --> 00:00:17.050 align:start size:94% position:6%
the Democratic Party
has to take a stronger stand

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:18.451 line:92%
against taking corporate money,

00:00:18.451 --> 00:00:20.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
or is that just the price
of doing business?

00:00:20.387 --> 00:00:23.723 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, look, I have been worried
for a very long time

00:00:23.723 --> 00:00:26.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
about the impact of money
in Washington.

00:00:26.259 --> 00:00:29.696 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know, money just
doesn't talk in Washington.

00:00:29.696 --> 00:00:33.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
It shouts. It screams.
It commands.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:35.969 align:start size:94% position:6%
But let's never lose sight
of the fact

00:00:35.969 --> 00:00:37.570 line:92%
that the Trump administration

00:00:37.570 --> 00:00:41.908
is the most corrupt
administration in our lifetime.

00:00:41.908 --> 00:00:45.111 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
We can't forget it.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.514 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
And...

00:00:47.514 --> 00:00:50.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
And think about
example after example --

00:00:50.417 --> 00:00:54.087
that, right now, the Saudis
can funnel money directly --

00:00:54.087 --> 00:00:58.425
indirectly into Trump's pockets
through the Trump Hotel...

00:00:58.425 --> 00:01:02.762
that the head of the
Environmental Protection Agency

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.598 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
is a coal lobbyist.

00:01:05.598 --> 00:01:07.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
And can I tell you
about Gary Cohn?

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:10.170 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Sure. Go for it.
-Yeah. So, here's the deal.

00:01:10.170 --> 00:01:12.105 line:92%
So, Trump is setting up --

00:01:12.105 --> 00:01:13.406 align:start size:94% position:6%
Trump is setting up
his administration.

00:01:13.406 --> 00:01:16.142 align:start size:94% position:6%
This is a year and a half
ago. He's setting up
his administration.

00:01:16.142 --> 00:01:17.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
He brings in all these
Goldman Sachs guys.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:21.915
I swear to you, they could
have opened a branch office

00:01:21.915 --> 00:01:24.451 align:start size:94% position:6%
of Goldman Sachs right there
in the White House.

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:26.386 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And it should be noted,
this is the same Goldman Sachs

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:28.755 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Donald Trump
railed against Hillary Clinton

00:01:28.755 --> 00:01:30.256 line:92%
for giving paid speeches to.

00:01:30.256 --> 00:01:30.990 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Exactly that one.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.992 align:start size:94% position:6%
Okay, so, he brings in
these Goldman Sachs people,

00:01:32.992 --> 00:01:34.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
but one of them
was very special.

00:01:34.828 --> 00:01:39.165
Gary Cohn was a major executive
at Goldman Sachs,

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:39.866 size:78% position:39% line:92%
and he is going to be

00:01:39.866 --> 00:01:42.635
the special advisor to the
President, economic advisor,

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:45.972 align:start size:94% position:6%
to help get
the tax laws changed.

00:01:45.972 --> 00:01:51.811
So Goldman Sachs gives Gary Cohn
a little gift on the way out --

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:55.181 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
$750 million.

00:01:55.181 --> 00:01:59.686 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think of it
as a sort of pre-bribe.

00:01:59.686 --> 00:02:04.491
And then Gary Cohn goes off
and writes the tax laws,

00:02:04.491 --> 00:02:06.226 line:92%
helps ram them through Congress,

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:10.663 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Goldman Sachs
makes billions of dollars

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.599 line:92%
off the change in the tax laws.

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:15.068 align:start size:94% position:6%
Let's call this out
for what it is.

00:02:15.068 --> 00:02:17.604 line:92%
Corruption. Pure and simple.

00:02:17.604 --> 00:02:19.506 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:23.009 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You mentioned --
You mentioned the Saudis.

00:02:23.009 --> 00:02:25.879
I also want to ask about this,
because I feel like we are so --

00:02:25.879 --> 00:02:27.947
We tend to get so focused
on what's happening in D.C.

00:02:27.947 --> 00:02:30.316
and what's specifically
happening with this presidency.

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:33.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
You wrote a letter today,
I believe,

00:02:33.019 --> 00:02:34.888 align:start size:94% position:6%
to the commander
of Central Command

00:02:34.888 --> 00:02:38.591 align:start size:94% position:6%
about this horrific bombing
in Yemen,

00:02:38.591 --> 00:02:41.761
a bombing that killed civilians,
killed children.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:46.866 line:92%
This is Saudis. This is the UAE.

00:02:46.866 --> 00:02:48.101 size:81% position:41% line:92%
But it is U.S.-backed,

00:02:48.101 --> 00:02:52.572
in that munitions, in that
refueling and intelligence.

00:02:52.572 --> 00:02:53.940 line:92%
Can you explain a little about

00:02:53.940 --> 00:02:55.942 align:start size:94% position:6%
what you asked for
in that letter?

00:02:55.942 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Sure.

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.646 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, this is an unfolding
humanitarian crisis,

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:04.584 size:81% position:41%
and the United States
is not dropping bombs,

00:03:04.584 --> 00:03:08.321 align:start size:94% position:6%
but it is helping the Saudis
with arms.

00:03:08.321 --> 00:03:10.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's helping the Saudis
with refueling.

00:03:10.456 --> 00:03:15.828
And it now appears it's helping
the Saudis target and pinpoint.

00:03:15.828 --> 00:03:17.730 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think that if the
United States is going to be

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:21.267
that directly involved
in a humanitarian crisis,

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.203 align:start size:94% position:6%
then the American people
have a right to know

00:03:23.203 --> 00:03:24.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
exactly what's going on.
-I agree with you,

00:03:24.837 --> 00:03:26.873 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm very glad
that you asked that question.

00:03:26.873 --> 00:03:28.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hopefully we get answers.
My last question.

00:03:28.741 --> 00:03:31.544 align:start size:94% position:6%
Obviously, we have
Justice Kavanaugh --

00:03:31.544 --> 00:03:32.478 line:92%
might-be Justice Kavanaugh.

00:03:32.478 --> 00:03:34.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
He is Trump's pick
for the Supreme Court.

00:03:34.480 --> 00:03:35.848 size:75% position:38% line:92%
-I hope not. Mm-hmm.

00:03:35.848 --> 00:03:37.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It strikes me
that maybe progressives

00:03:37.817 --> 00:03:40.320 align:start size:94% position:6%
are not making
the same push to stop this

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:41.554 line:92%
that they had made to, say,

00:03:41.554 --> 00:03:43.856 size:81% position:41%
stop the repeal of the
Affordable Care Act.

00:03:43.856 --> 00:03:45.525 line:92%
Do you think this is something

00:03:45.525 --> 00:03:46.926 align:start size:94% position:6%
that enough effort's
being put behind,

00:03:46.926 --> 00:03:48.861 align:start size:94% position:6%
or do you think
it's basically a done deal

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's going to be
our next justice?

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:53.366 size:81% position:41%
-So, you know, look,
it is not a done deal.

00:03:53.366 --> 00:03:56.135 align:start size:94% position:6%
Donald Trump
has made his nomination,

00:03:56.135 --> 00:04:01.274
and he picks somebody off a list
that has been prescreened,

00:04:01.274 --> 00:04:06.112
prescreened by not one but two
right-wing extremist groups.

00:04:06.112 --> 00:04:07.680 line:92%
-I will say it's just refreshing

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:10.483
that anyone screens someone
that Donald Trump picked.

00:04:10.483 --> 00:04:14.554
Usually he just opens the door
and, like, lets in 15 people.

00:04:14.554 --> 00:04:16.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
-But not this time.
-Okay. Gotcha.

00:04:16.522 --> 00:04:19.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Not this time,
because one of the groups,

00:04:19.525 --> 00:04:22.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
the founder of the group's
number-one goal

00:04:22.695 --> 00:04:24.964 line:92%
is to overturn Roe vs. Wade.

00:04:24.964 --> 00:04:26.766 align:start size:94% position:6%
So think about
what that screen is,

00:04:26.766 --> 00:04:28.301 line:92%
that he made it onto this list.

00:04:28.301 --> 00:04:29.435 line:92%
The other group, very hostile

00:04:29.435 --> 00:04:33.706 align:start size:94% position:6%
to government protecting
healthcare for all Americans.

00:04:33.706 --> 00:04:37.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, just last night,
I was in Boston,

00:04:37.543 --> 00:04:41.547 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I got to say we were doing
a Rise Up for Roe,

00:04:41.547 --> 00:04:43.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, out there
in the fight.

00:04:43.983 --> 00:04:47.487 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because here's the deal
about this.

00:04:47.487 --> 00:04:52.725
I remember the night that
Donald Trump was sworn in,

00:04:52.725 --> 00:04:55.795 line:92%
and I remember thinking they --

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:57.030 line:92%
"Healthcare could disappear

00:04:57.030 --> 00:05:02.368 align:start size:94% position:6%
for tens of millions
of Americans by next week

00:05:02.368 --> 00:05:04.704
because they now have
the House, they have the Senate,

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have the White House,
they have the votes."

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:12.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
And, I thought, "What have we
got left to fight with?"

00:05:12.512 --> 00:05:16.015 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the answer is
all we got left is each other.

00:05:16.015 --> 00:05:20.386
We've got the ability to come
together to raise our voices,

00:05:20.386 --> 00:05:21.788 line:92%
to be strong, to fight back,

00:05:21.788 --> 00:05:24.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
to make sure that
this Washington hears us.

00:05:24.324 --> 00:05:26.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And over healthcare,
I'm thinking,

00:05:26.459 --> 00:05:27.593 line:92%
"Where do we get this army?"

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:31.497 size:84% position:42%
And the next morning
after the inauguration,

00:05:31.497 --> 00:05:32.899 line:92%
anyone remember the women?

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:37.904 align:start size:94% position:6%
The largest protest rally
in the history of the world.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.439 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:41.507 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
So...I get it.

00:05:41.507 --> 00:05:43.710 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:43.710 --> 00:05:46.279 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
You bet.

00:05:46.279 --> 00:05:48.414 line:92%
Here's what I see happening.

00:05:48.414 --> 00:05:50.817 align:start size:94% position:6%
Yeah, Donald Trump
is on the attack,

00:05:50.817 --> 00:05:51.884 line:92%
and he's trying to roll back

00:05:51.884 --> 00:05:54.654 align:start size:94% position:6%
protection for women,
Roe vs. Wade,

00:05:54.654 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
probably roll back
a lot of other protections

00:05:57.190 --> 00:05:59.192 align:start size:94% position:6%
with Judge Kavanaugh's
nomination.

00:05:59.192 --> 00:06:03.596
He would be the deciding vote
on all of these critical issues.

00:06:03.596 --> 00:06:05.965 line:92%
But at the very same moment

00:06:05.965 --> 00:06:08.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Donald Trump
is trying to do this,

00:06:08.735 --> 00:06:11.070 line:92%
democracy itself is changing.

00:06:11.070 --> 00:06:13.439 align:start size:94% position:6%
It changed with
the Women's March.

00:06:13.439 --> 00:06:16.409 size:81% position:41%
It changed when people
went to the airports

00:06:16.409 --> 00:06:19.379 size:88% position:44%
after Trump tried to put
a Muslim ban in place.

00:06:19.379 --> 00:06:22.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
It changed when people
went down to Washington --

00:06:22.949 --> 00:06:26.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
the mamas of babies
with complex medical needs,

00:06:26.819 --> 00:06:27.787 line:92%
people who use wheelchairs,

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:31.290
who got right up in the face
of the Republican senators.

00:06:31.290 --> 00:06:35.061
It keeps changing as more people
come off the sidelines.

00:06:35.061 --> 00:06:39.132
15-year-olds and 16-year-olds
after the shooting in Florida

00:06:39.132 --> 00:06:39.999 line:92%
said, "I'm in this fight.

00:06:39.999 --> 00:06:42.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm going to make sure
my government hears from me."

00:06:42.468 --> 00:06:46.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
So that's what it takes.
And I believe we can do this.

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.107
-All right.
Well, have fun at work tomorrow.

00:06:48.107 --> 00:06:49.709 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I will.
-I hope you enjoy your return.

00:06:49.709 --> 00:06:51.477 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being back here.

00:06:51.477 --> 00:06:53.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-You bet.
-It's always a pleasure.

